From: Uke recovery maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libmodprobe: deny automatic storage writers in recovery

The matched Uke stock recovery module list loads charger_partition, whose
probe schedules raw charger-partition writes, and ufs_ffu, which schedules
firmware-update work. Deny both before any loader path can insert them.
Force this denial when the packaged recovery executable is present, even
when a caller disables OEM blocklists. Preserve normal-boot behavior and
the stock blocklist. Existing dependency checks skip dependent drivers.

diff --git a/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp b/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
--- a/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
+++ b/libmodprobe/libmodprobe.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <sys/stat.h>
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #include <sys/wait.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <map>
@@ -401,6 +402,17 @@ Modprobe::Modprobe(const std::vector<std::string>& base_paths, const std::string loa
         ParseCfg(base_path + "/modules.blocklist", blocklist_callback);
     }
 
+    // Recovery retains its packaged ramdisk. Apply the mandatory denial here
+    // so OEM ramdisk lists and use_blocklist=false cannot admit these drivers.
+    // charger_partition schedules raw partition writes on probe; ufs_ffu
+    // schedules UFS firmware-update work. Also reject their hard dependents.
+    // A normal Android ramdisk does not contain the recovery executable.
+    if (access("/system/bin/recovery", F_OK) == 0) {
+        blocklist_enabled = true;
+        module_blocklist_.emplace("charger_partition");
+        module_blocklist_.emplace("ufs_ffu");
+    }
+
     ParseKernelCmdlineOptions();
 }
 
